{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba ../native-source/config.go | sed -n '314,350p'\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,jsonschema\nart='2e3b56209cca43599ce8a2d6edaed0bb'\ns={'action':'review','artifact_id':art,'rationale':'Whole-artifact review inspected the captured plan/harness and raw completed execution 7e6a028e01ac489a91c5a9da73ce81b9. A complete local measurement exists, but harness configuration violates the source validation rule; record this concrete applicability issue before repair and fresh execution. No broader history or application conclusion is supported.','sources':[{'id':'src-default-and-valid-config','file':'config.go','start_line':314,'end_line':375,'kind':'code_observation'}],'review_items':[{'target_id':'obligation-expired-contact-lease','aspect':'applicability','status':'no_issue_found','source_ids':['src-lease-contract','src-lease','src-pipeline-contract'],'rationale':'The obligation is conditional on no contact with a required remote voter and an already-expired prior marker. The public lease contract supports role loss in that condition. Counting a real negative heartbeat as contact is an alternative outside the no-response antecedent. This interpretation does not require every pipeline error to imply no receiver processing; the harness independently supplies no receiver worker.','counterevidence':[],'limitations':['Conditional local prefix is not established by an election history.','Harness configuration validity is challenged separately below.']},{'target_id':'obligation-expired-contact-lease','aspect':'decomposition','status':'no_issue_found','source_ids':['src-lease','src-inmem-pipeline-timeout','src-pipeline-reply','src-replication-progress','src-verify'],'rationale':'Real timeout publication -> real pipeline consumer -> contact marker -> actual lease decision addresses the selected A2 relation. The oracle observes role after lease consumption, not merely the response-interface mismatch. Ordinary timeout is an independent comparison. Even if this obligation held, stale reads or incorrect commits could still arise through other mechanisms; it is not sufficient for overall correctness.','counterevidence':[],'limitations':['Fallback replication, incoming RPCs, heartbeat and VerifyLeader workers are omitted and may alter full-node role duration.','No observed application endpoint or automatic lease scheduling.']},{'target_id':art,'aspect':'checker_correspondence','status':'revision_needed','source_ids':['src-default-and-valid-config','src-lease-contract','src-lease','src-inmem-pipeline-timeout','src-pipeline-reply'],'rationale':'Saved checker selects independent lease_result events, correlates operation with prefix and completed events, and asserts State == Follower. Raw execution has no parse errors, correlated results 3 and 7, pipeline command timed out with same_request=true, actual contact refresh and Leader result, plus ordinary timeout unchanged contact and Follower result. Completion is awaited before result; receiver processing/replies are structurally absent; result is not a prerequisite. However saved harness uses DefaultConfig (HeartbeatTimeout and ElectionTimeout 1s), sets LeaderLeaseTimeout to 2s, then bypasses ValidateConfig by storing config directly. config.go rejects lease greater than heartbeat. This prevents attribution to a supported configuration even though the local measurement is intact. Repair by setting HeartbeatTimeout and ElectionTimeout to at least 2s, calling ValidateConfig before execution, retaining lease 2s, prior contact 4s, oracle, prerequisites and actual transport paths. Fresh execution and focused review must resolve this issue; a source-only assurance is insufficient.','counterevidence':['src-default-and-valid-config: DefaultConfig supplies HeartbeatTimeout=1s; ValidateConfig rejects LeaderLeaseTimeout > HeartbeatTimeout and ElectionTimeout < HeartbeatTimeout.'],'limitations':['Initial Leader state and expired marker remain explicit constructed premises after configuration repair.','State reports local role; this is not a claim of global leadership or a client completion.']}], 'feedback':{'ref_ids':[art,'7e6a028e01ac489a91c5a9da73ce81b9'],'answered':'Both formal scenarios reached result events and the pipeline scenario violated the encoded local lease comparison. Whole-artifact review found invalid heartbeat/lease configuration, so supported-input attribution remains pending despite the complete measurement.','remaining':['Repair heartbeat/election durations and invoke ValidateConfig; rerun same oracle and review the corrected artifact.','Legal elected-cluster prefix, automatic scheduling and application consequences remain outside current evidence.'],'understanding':'unchanged','rationale':'Prioritize the concrete harness legality repair before extending history or changing the obligation. No map or oracle change is needed.'}}\njsonschema.validate(s,json.load(open('../native-submission.schema.json')))\njson.dump(s,open('submission-review-config.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
